    "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a 21-layer planar multilayer filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Stack sequence: Air | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | Fused silica. Initialize all layer thicknesses as quarter-wave optical thickness at 267.5 nm wavelength (t_HfO2 = 267.5/(4*2.1) ≈ 31.8 nm, t_SiO2 = 267.5/(4*1.5) ≈ 44.6 nm). Optimize using bounded differential evolution with penalty term proportional to deviation from quarter-wave optical path lengths during first 50 generations, then allow free thickness variation. Wavelength bands: maximize transmittance 255-280 nm, suppress transmittance 300-700 nm and 700-1100 nm. No metal layers. Total layer count exactly 21. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 255–280 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Transmittance in 300–700 nm; Transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum 30 layers; No metal layers; Only conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials.",
